WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.459
Welcome to Module 4, Installation
Qualification, or IQ.

2
00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:09.357
We continue with the fictional V-201 oral-
liquid mixing vessel.

3
00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:12.400
The design review described what was
intended.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.083
Now the team compares the installed system
with the accepted

5
00:00:16.203 --> 00:00:18.955
design and manufacturer recommendations.

6
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:23.768
Every identifier and observation in this
module is invented for training.

7
00:00:23.888 --> 00:00:26.448
No real equipment has been qualified.

8
00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:29.892
A drawing shows a temperature sensor
connection.

9
00:00:30.012 --> 00:00:34.236
A walkdown identifies which sensor is
installed at that connection.

10
00:00:34.356 --> 00:00:38.729
An operational challenge examines how the
assembled loop behaves.

11
00:00:38.849 --> 00:00:40.849
These answer different questions.

12
00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:44.937
Finding the correct tag does not
demonstrate alarm response,

13
00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:47.212
and a successful alarm test does

14
00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:50.361
not repair missing material
identification.

15
00:00:50.481 --> 00:00:54.129
Keep each conclusion tied to the evidence
actually obtained.

16
00:00:54.749 --> 00:00:58.278
For our case, the installation boundary
includes the vessel,

17
00:00:58.398 --> 00:01:01.172
agitator, outlet components, instruments

18
00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:03.425
and defined utility connections.

19
00:01:03.545 --> 00:01:07.364
The upstream utility plant has its own
qualification scope.

20
00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:10.534
Record where one system ends and another
begins.

21
00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:12.654
A qualified water system does

22
00:01:12.774 --> 00:01:16.127
not automatically prove that a new branch
has the correct

23
00:01:16.247 --> 00:01:19.247
connection or that its delivered water is
suitable.

24
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:23.046
The teaching conclusion is limited to
installation

25
00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:26.089
evidence reviewed against the defined
baseline.

26
00:01:26.209 --> 00:01:29.003
It is not permission to manufacture a
batch.

27
00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:33.369
Operational and performance verification
remain separate needs.

28
00:01:33.489 --> 00:01:36.497
Where stages are combined in an approved
approach,

29
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:40.009
the underlying evidence questions still
remain visible.

30
00:01:40.129 --> 00:01:42.987
Your first activity separates installation

31
00:01:43.107 --> 00:01:46.435
observations from claims that require
later studies.
